# Do not change master directly

`master` is not a working branch. Do not edit files, stage, or commit while `HEAD` is `master`.

Before any edit or commit, check the current branch.

## Already on another branch

Stay there. Commit on that branch.

## Currently on master, with uncommitted changes

1. `git stash push -m "<why>"`
2. Create and switch to a new branch. Do not reuse `master`.
3. `git stash pop`
4. Commit on the new branch.

## Currently on master, before starting edits

Create and switch to a new branch first, then edit and commit there. Do not stash an empty tree.

## After the commit

Leave the work on the new branch. Do not merge it into `master`, and do not open a merge request, unless the user explicitly asks.

If they ask to land it, either merge that branch into `master`, or push the branch and let them open the merge request by hand. Do not push or merge on your own.
